      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "This is observable with anything that runs during the removal steps, right? In Chromium, that's `blur` events (https://chromestatus.com/feature/5128696823545856) , but I think the spec doesn't suffer from this legacy behavior. So probably there's no way to observe this change \"spec\" wise, and maybe that's good enough.\r\n\r\nI guess the only other way this would be observable would be if https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#reset-the-form-owner queued any microtasks whose execution order could be observed with respect to the various [`disconnectedCallback`s that get queued](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#ref-for-enqueue-a-custom-element-callback-reaction%E2%91%A1). But that algorithm doesn't do that, so I think we're good.",
